Acuiting Score System

Things to think about: Nurses experience, Proximity of the rooms

Hemodynamic Status:
    Stable:
    - No vasopressors, MAP >65, No active bleeding → Score: 0-1
    Moderate Instability
    - Single vasopressor (low dose)/ Occasional fluid bolus → Score: 2
    Unstable
    - Multiple pressors OR Titration, IABP/Impella → Score 3-4
----------------------------------------
Cardiac Status:
- Stable Rhythm
    NSR / Controlled Afib/ SB(Asymptomatic 45-60) → Score: 0
- Arrhythmia Risk
    AF with RVR, Frequent PVCs, Frequent NSVT
High Risk
    VT,VF history, TVP(Temporary Pacemaker) → Score: 3
-------------------------------------------
Respiratory Status
- Room Air/ Low O2 requirement
    Nasal Prongs <= 4L → Score: 0
Moderate Support
    HFNC/CPAP/BIPAP → Score: 2
Critical
    Mechanical Ventilation, Intubated/ ARDS → Score: 3- 4
-------------------------------------------
Neurological Status:
    A&O x 3 → Score: 0
    Altered/ Confused/ Delirium → Score: 1-2
    Critical/ Sedated/GCS < 8 → Score: 3
------------------------------------------
Medication Complexity
- Minimal   
    PO meds only → Score: 0
- Moderate
    IV meds/ Insulin Drip → Score: 1-2
- High Complexity
    Multiple Titratable drips → Score: 3-4
--------------------------------------------
Lines/Devices
- Basic
    No IV/Devices → Score: 0
- Moderate
    Central line/ Arterial line → Score: 1-2
Complex
    IABP/ CRRT/ ECMO → Score: 3-4
---------------------------------------------
Lab Monitoring/Instability
- Routine
    Daily Labs → Score: 0
- Frequent Monitoring 
    Electrolyte Replacement → Score: 1-2
- Critical
    ABGs,Unstable Labs → Score: 3
